meta {
  name: 3 Create profession — MUST be 404 or 405
  seq: 3
  type: http
}
post {
  url: {{professionUrl}}/api/v1/professions
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "name": "Smuggled Profession"
  }
}
tests {
  test("route is GONE — 404 or 405, never 201", function () {
    expect([404, 405]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });
}
docs {
  **This route was deleted, not role-gated** (ADR-025, threat T-007). It is kept in the collection as a
  negative check: a `201` here is a regression.

  Why deleted: Identity's role allow-list is exactly `{Provider, Customer}` — there is **no admin role** to
  gate on. The only implementable check would still have let any self-registered provider write global
  reference data read by every user. Professions are seeded and no shipped flow creates one, so nothing was
  lost.

  Before removal, both a Provider **and** a Customer token got `201` and wrote to the global catalogue.

  You should get **405** (the path still serves `GET`, so `POST` is method-not-allowed).
}
